 <section class="engine wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE SAME ENGINE. A SMALLER WINDOW.</p><h2>Real search.<br>Not a pretend demo.</h2><p>The website uses the same Rust search core as the desktop app, through a small API adapter. No hard-coded results, no made-up answers, and no hidden switch to an unrelated demo.</p></div><ol class="engine-steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Your question.</h3><p>A few words, a whole question, or something you’ve been meaning to look up.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>The Sreon engine.</h3><p>It asks existing web-search sources and returns links, titles, and short excerpts. Recent results may come from a brief in-memory cache.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Back to the original.</h3><p>Every result links to its website. You choose what to read, watch, or explore next.</p></div></li></ol></section>
 <section class="privacy wrap" id="privacy"><div><p class="eyebrow privacy-address">sreon<a href="/site/notes/" class="quiet-colon" aria-label="Open notes">:</a>//privacy</p><h2>How privacy<br>actually works here<span class="brand-period">.</span></h2><p>Plain language. Not a promise<br>that the internet can’t keep.</p></div><div class="privacy-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Your searches go somewhere.</h3><p>This demo sends your query to the Sreon API. The engine asks external search providers for results. The website host and those providers may process connection details.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Your preferences stay here.</h3><p>This page stores your theme in this browser. It has no analytics script or advertising tracker. The hosting service may keep its own request logs.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>A website is still a website.</h3><p>Following a result takes you to that site, with its own cookies and privacy practices. Sreon is not a VPN or an anonymity service.</p></div></article></div></section>
 <section class="questions wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">A FEW THINGS WORTH KNOWING</p><h2>Just the<br>straight answers.</h2></div><div><details><summary>Is this a whole browser inside a website?</summary><p>No. This is a small window into Sreon’s search engine. The desktop app handles actual browsing using your system’s webview. Here, results take you to the original websites.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need an account to search?</summary><p>No Sreon account is required. The public search service has request limits to keep it available, and external search sources may sometimes be unavailable.</p></details><details><summary>Does Sreon have its own search index?</summary><p>Not currently. The Rust engine retrieves results from existing online sources. Sreon is open about that distinction instead of claiming to crawl the whole web.</p></details><details><summary>What stays on this device?</summary><p>This page remembers your light or dark theme locally. It doesn’t save a search-history list in your browser. Queries still go to the search service and its providers; hosting services may keep connection logs.</p></details></div></section>
